  "content": {
    "id": "p26-q52-63-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "52",
    "prompt": "Solve the following equations.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p26-q52",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$5^x+5^{-x}=3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\log_5\\left(\\dfrac{3\\pm\\sqrt5}{2}\\right)$.\n\nMultiply by $5^x$ to form a quadratic in $5^x$; both resulting exponential values are positive.",
          "worked": "Since $5^x>0$, multiply by $5^x$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}5^{2x}+1&=3(5^x)\\\\(5^x)^2-3(5^x)+1&=0\\\\5^x&=\\frac{3\\pm\\sqrt{9-4}}{2}\\\\5^x&=\\frac{3\\pm\\sqrt5}{2}\\\\x&=\\log_5\\left(\\frac{3\\pm\\sqrt5}{2}\\right)\\end{align*}$$\n\nBoth values of $5^x$ are positive, so both solutions are valid.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 70
      },
      {
        "id": "p26-q53",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$4(9^x)+3^{x+1}=1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-\\log_3 4$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}4(3^x)^2+3(3^x)-1&=0\\\\(4(3^x)-1)(3^x+1)&=0\\\\3^x&=\\frac14\\quad\\text{or}\\quad -1\\end{align*}$$\n\nReject $3^x=-1$ because $3^x>0$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\log_3\\left(\\frac14\\right)\\\\x&=-\\log_3 4\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 54
      },
      {
        "id": "p26-q54",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$2^{2x+1}=1-2^x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-1$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}2(2^x)^2+2^x-1&=0\\\\(2(2^x)-1)(2^x+1)&=0\\\\2^x&=\\frac12\\quad\\text{or}\\quad -1\\end{align*}$$\n\nReject $2^x=-1$ because $2^x>0$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}2^x&=2^{-1}\\\\x&=-1\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p26-q55",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$2^{2x}-3(2^x)-10=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\log_2 5$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(2^x)^2-3(2^x)-10&=0\\\\(2^x-5)(2^x+2)&=0\\\\2^x&=5\\quad\\text{or}\\quad -2\\end{align*}$$\n\nReject $2^x=-2$ because $2^x>0$.\n\n$$x=\\log_2 5$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p26-q56",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$e^{2x}-10e^x+21=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\ln 3$ or $x=\\ln 7$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(e^x)^2-10e^x+21&=0\\\\(e^x-3)(e^x-7)&=0\\\\e^x&=3\\quad\\text{or}\\quad 7\\\\x&=\\ln 3\\quad\\text{or}\\quad\\ln 7\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p26-q57",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$9^x-3^{x+1}=9$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\log_3\\left(\\dfrac{3+3\\sqrt5}{2}\\right)$.\n\nSolve the quadratic in $3^x$ and retain its positive root.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(3^x)^2-3(3^x)-9&=0\\\\3^x&=\\frac{3\\pm\\sqrt{9+36}}{2}\\\\3^x&=\\frac{3\\pm3\\sqrt5}{2}\\end{align*}$$\n\nReject $\\dfrac{3-3\\sqrt5}{2}$ because $3^x>0$.\n\n$$x=\\log_3\\left(\\frac{3+3\\sqrt5}{2}\\right)$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "p26-q58",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$25^x+5^x=12$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\log_5 3$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(5^x)^2+5^x-12&=0\\\\(5^x+4)(5^x-3)&=0\\\\5^x&=-4\\quad\\text{or}\\quad 3\\end{align*}$$\n\nReject $5^x=-4$ because $5^x>0$.\n\n$$x=\\log_5 3$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p26-q59",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "$4^{x+2}+2^{x+2}-1=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\log_2\\left(\\dfrac{\\sqrt5-1}{8}\\right)$.\n\nUse index laws to form a quadratic in $2^x$ and retain its positive root.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}16(2^x)^2+4(2^x)-1&=0\\\\2^x&=\\frac{-4\\pm\\sqrt{16+64}}{32}\\\\2^x&=\\frac{-1\\pm\\sqrt5}{8}\\end{align*}$$\n\nReject $\\dfrac{-1-\\sqrt5}{8}$ because $2^x>0$.\n\n$$x=\\log_2\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt5-1}{8}\\right)$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "p26-q60",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "i",
        "prompt": "$4^x-6(2^x)+5=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=0$ or $x=\\log_2 5$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(2^x)^2-6(2^x)+5&=0\\\\(2^x-1)(2^x-5)&=0\\\\2^x&=1\\quad\\text{or}\\quad 5\\\\x&=0\\quad\\text{or}\\quad\\log_2 5\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p26-q61",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "j",
        "prompt": "$9^x-3^{x+1}+2=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=0$ or $x=\\log_3 2$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(3^x)^2-3(3^x)+2&=0\\\\(3^x-1)(3^x-2)&=0\\\\3^x&=1\\quad\\text{or}\\quad 2\\\\x&=0\\quad\\text{or}\\quad\\log_3 2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p26-q62",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "k",
        "prompt": "$25^x-5^{x+1}=6$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\log_5 6$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(5^x)^2-5(5^x)-6&=0\\\\(5^x-6)(5^x+1)&=0\\\\5^x&=6\\quad\\text{or}\\quad -1\\end{align*}$$\n\nReject $5^x=-1$ because $5^x>0$.\n\n$$x=\\log_5 6$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p26-q63",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "l",
        "prompt": "$4^{2x}-6(2^{2x})+5=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=0$ or $x=\\dfrac12\\log_2 5$.\n\nFactor as a quadratic in $2^{2x}$, then divide the logarithmic exponent equation by 2.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(2^{2x})^2-6(2^{2x})+5&=0\\\\(2^{2x}-1)(2^{2x}-5)&=0\\\\2^{2x}&=1\\quad\\text{or}\\quad 5\\\\2x&=0\\quad\\text{or}\\quad\\log_2 5\\\\x&=0\\quad\\text{or}\\quad\\frac12\\log_2 5\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      }
    ]
  },
